ADT - abstract data types
=========================

Implementation of data structures and abstract data types in C.

01 - LIST
=========

The List ADT stores integer values in order. It is implemented with a
singly-linked list. The node and list structure are private to the library;
use the functions in libadt.h to work with a list.

Create and destroy
------------------

List *list_create(void);       Create an empty list. Returns NULL on failure.
void list_destroy(List *list); Free the list and all of its items.

Add values
----------

int list_add_front(List *list, int value);  Add a value at the front.
int list_add_end(List *list, int value);    Add a value at the end.

Both functions return 1 on success and 0 if the list is NULL or memory
allocation fails.

Remove values
-------------

int list_remove_front(List *list, int *value);       Remove the first value.
int list_remove_end(List *list, int *value);         Remove the last value.
int list_remove_index(List *list, size_t index, int *value);

The index is zero-based. If value is not NULL, the removed value is stored
there. These functions return 1 if an item was removed and 0 if the list is
NULL, empty, or the index is out of range.

List size
---------

size_t list_size(const List *list);  Return the number of values in the list.

list_size returns 0 when list is NULL.
